    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1052">

                <pb facs="0995" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1834</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to your
                    personal note of October 12, 1915, relative to the alleged shipment by parcels
                    post from New York to Germany and Austria of mineral slag, rubber, and shoes, I
                    beg to advise you that the Department is now in receipt of a letter from the
                    Postmaster General, communicating a report from the postmaster at New York, in
                    which it is stated that no parcels containing printing material compound or
                    rubber stamp material have been shipped through that office to Germany; but that
                    mineral slag, not being included in the contraband list of your Government,
                    parcels said to contain that product have been sent by parcels post to
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>The postmaster stated also, that shoes being on the conditional contraband list
                    have not been considered as prohibited and that parcels containing shoes have
                    been shipped to private parties in Germany and Austria.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
